> I've heard that one could fashion armor from these scales but I'll be damned
> if I could figure out how. In the off chance I ever get the opportunity
> again, how does one forge armor from scales?

Wear them, and read a scroll of enchant armor.  Added tip: bless the scroll
first to get some extra plusses on the resulting armor.

> Are there any scales that create better armor than others?

Why, yes.  Orange is one of the least useful as dragon armors go, because
the resistance it confers (sleep) is obtainable so many other ways.
However, if you have no other dragon scales handy, it's much better than
any alternative armor, such as dwarven chain.  Dragon scale mail armor
is both light and very good in AC, no matter what color.

Gray and silver are the most popular scales.  The most useful of these two
typically depends on what class you are, and what other equipment you've
found.

You would probably benefit greatly from reading spoilers, if you're 
willing to be spoiled.  Check the links section off of www.nethack.org.

